"""The panels' debriefs (Phase 5 spec 15.3), as the agents wrote them, and the questions each should miss, as graded
by hand: the baseline's six (b1-b6, played on Phase 4's game in the review round) and the gate's twelve, on Phase 5's
game (g1-g6 in gate G5 run 1, h1-h6 in run 2). tests/test_playtest.py pins tools/playtest_grade.py's rubric to them.

b1-b3, g1-g3 and h1-h3 played apple-terminal-26, b4-b6, g4-g6 and h4-h6 kitty. b2 never started a game (its run also
fails task-1:stuck:menu, from its log), so it answers from the manual, and guesses. b6's (b) is right in other words
("shot slots are free", "bombs you can still use"). Graded whole from their logs (not in the tree), b2 fails and the
other 17 pass. h1-h6 did every task; h1 guessed one key, Esc at command 124 (in play, whose footer names only P),
which is counted, not failed.

(c) is graded against what each run's screens showed (gate G6). TELLS says whether any did show a shooter in its tell
pose: none did. Every run's play ended in waves 1-3, where only scouts fire, and pellets come with no tell. Each log of
b1-b6 and g1-g6 was replayed (gfix-grade, every screen matching its hash), and no command ended on a screen with a
tell; h1-h6's logs record it (truth "tell" false on every command). So an honest answer is "no warning, the `!` is the
shot": b3, b5, g5, g6, h1-h4 and h6 say so, and each is right. g6, h1 and h6 guess or suppose a colour or flash, and
h4 a telegraph it missed: hedges, not assertions. h1 and h4 deny a list of cues ("I never saw an invader change its
look, blink, or show a marker before it fired"), and the denial reaches every item. b1, b4, b6, g1-g4 and h5 describe
the pellet leaving a scout's middle (`\\W/` to `\\!/`; h5's `/W\\` to `/!\\`) as a change of shape, which is what
their screens showed, and are right too (g3 quotes the tip, then shown at a diver's wobble, but its `!` at the invader
is what it saw). b2 gives no observation of a shot ("I never saw a wave"), so its (c) is wrong.
"""

